    "narrative": "The **Austin Waves** lineup for July 26th is anchored by **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88), who stands as our premier play today. His matchup against Reynaldo L\u00f3pez is highly favorable; the combination of a +16% park factor and the offensive boost from hitting in the 3-hole creates an elite ceiling for power and run production. **Drake Baldwin** (71.83) and **Jackson Merrill** (71.56) also present as strong pillars. **Drake Baldwin** benefits from a high-leverage leadoff spot against a hittable starter in Baz, while **Jackson Merrill** leverages a high efficiency score driven by a significant platoon advantage and a favorable SP matchup, making him a high-probability candidate for a multi-category contribution.\n\nPlatoon advantages are driving several mid-tier starts today. **Denzer Guzman** (53.32) is a value play, as the +19% edge against a soft starter like Whisenhunt combined with wind-out conditions compensates for his lower spot in the order. Conversely, **Heliot Ramos** (55.10) sits on the lower end of our starting threshold despite a solid base projection; while the wind-out conditions are helpful, the heavy emphasis on SB-efficiency requires us to be cautious with players whose primary value is strictly power-hitting in this matchup. **Sam Antonacci** (48.70) remains in the lineup to protect our SB volume, even though the tough matchup against Blanco suppresses his raw efficiency score.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (47.58), who narrowly missed the cut. While he possesses the talent to outperform his projection, the negative platoon split against a lefty like Drake\u2014compounded by his position in the bottom third of the order\u2014made him a sub-optimal choice compared to the higher floor provided by our current starters. We are prioritizing the high-efficiency, park-boosted profiles of **Dominic Smith** and **Andy Pages** today to maximize our return on game caps. Investors should note that while most of our lineup is set, any late-breaking weather alerts or lineup shifts for **Drake Baldwin** or **Jacob Wilson** could force a pivot, but for now, the data strongly supports this configuration for an optimal Roto push.",
